## Pull request overview

Adds a new accessibility feature that moves keyboard focus to the workbench part under the mouse cursor after a short debounce, implementing a focus-follows-mouse behavior (issue #93772). The contribution is wired into the accessibility contribution registry alongside the existing unfocused-view dimming contribution and is configured by two new application-scoped settings.

**Changes:**
- Introduces `FocusFollowsMouseContribution` with mouse listeners on the side bar, panel, auxiliary bar, and per-editor-group elements, debounced and guarded against held buttons and visible context menus.
- Adds `accessibility.focusFollowsMouse.enabled` and `accessibility.focusFollowsMouse.delay` configuration keys.
- Adds unit tests covering enable/disable, the guards, runtime toggling, editor group lifecycle, and custom delays.

### Reviewed changes

Copilot reviewed 4 out of 4 changed files in this pull request and generated 4 comments.

| File | Description |
| ---- | ----------- |
| src/vs/workbench/contrib/accessibility/browser/accessibility.contribution.ts | Registers the new contribution at `AfterRestored`. |
| src/vs/workbench/contrib/accessibility/browser/accessibilityConfiguration.ts | Declares the two new settings (enabled/delay) and their descriptions. |
| src/vs/workbench/contrib/accessibility/browser/focusFollowsMouseContribution.ts | Implements the focus-follows-mouse behavior with guards and listener lifecycle. |
| src/vs/workbench/contrib/accessibility/test/browser/focusFollowsMouseContribution.test.ts | Adds tests with test doubles for the layout/editor groups services. |



